## Context

Brain dump from operator: "autoresearch — universal the prompt".

The project currently carries several bespoke prompts (inventory,
scenarios, skill, census, rag, decomposed, sourced, multiturn) and
the ablation machinery under `prompt_modules/` mixes and matches
persona/overview/method fragments per sweep. Each variant is a
hand-crafted artifact, tuned by feel, and we have no principled way
to search the prompt space for a single "universal" prompt that
performs well across models and conditions.

Autoresearch (https://github.com/autoresearch/autoresearch or similar
automated prompt-search tooling — identify the exact project) offers
automated prompt optimization / search. The hypothesis: feed our
measurements.jsonl back as a signal and let Autoresearch converge on
one prompt that dominates the current hand-tuned set across models.

This is a research spike, not a committed implementation.

## Actions

1. Identify the specific "Autoresearch" tool the operator means
   (candidates: the Autoresearch project, DSPy's bootstrap/optimize,
   promptbreeder, OPRO). Confirm with operator before spending cycles.
2. Read the tool's docs and one end-to-end example. Note the
   optimization target format (metric, dataset, eval harness).
3. Sketch how our `measurements.jsonl` + method-level accuracy scores
   could serve as the optimization signal. Does the tool need a
   differentiable metric, a scalar score, or pairwise judgments?
4. Prototype on one sweep cell (e.g. the inventory prompt on a small
   model set) and compare the Autoresearch-produced prompt against
   the current hand-tuned baseline using the existing verification
   sweep.
5. Write up: is "one universal prompt" even the right frame, or does
   the tool just give us better per-condition prompts?

## Test

A notebook or short script that runs the optimizer on one condition,
reports the optimized prompt, and runs it through the existing
evaluation to produce a before/after accuracy comparison.

## Exit criteria

- Spike report in `docs/` or as a note on this ticket answering:
  can Autoresearch produce a prompt that beats our hand-tuned
  baseline on at least one sweep condition, and at what cost?
- Decision recorded: adopt, defer, or reject. If adopt, open a
  follow-up ticket for production integration.
